// Passing failures on. `attempt` can start a `var`, a `return`, or a line
// of its own when the result isn't needed. Each passes the call's
// failures on, so this action's `fails` list holds every failure of
// `check_kitchen` and `reserve_cakes`.
//
// Actions call other actions in their domain by bare name. Functions
// can't call actions: a function is pure, while an action is an
// operation that, in later areas, reads and writes data.

/// Takes an order for `asked` cakes, if the kitchen can bake them and
/// the shelf has them.
action place_order(
    left: Stock,
    asked: CakeCount,
    load: HourlyLoad,
    ovens: OvensOn
) fails CakeSoldOut, KitchenBusy, OvenDown -> CakeCount {
    attempt check_kitchen(load, ovens)
    return attempt reserve_cakes(left, asked)
}
